    "description": "Deployed staging API (API Gateway -> Cognito authorizer -> Lambda). Auth is a real Cognito ID token, not a header \u2014 set this collection's Authorization tab to OAuth 2.0 with your User Pool's token URL/client id/scope (same config you already verified working on the Transactions folder), then every request below inherits it automatically.\n\nCreate requests have a test script that captures the returned id into a collection variable (accountId, transactionId, locationId, tagId, categoryId, budgetId, attachmentId) so folders can be run top-to-bottom with the Collection Runner.\n\nThe `userId` variable is NOT your own identity (that comes from the token) \u2014 it's only used where the API needs a *target* user id, e.g. adding another member to a budget.",
